Define $B_1 = A_1$ and $B_n = A_n \\ (A_1 union ... union A_(n-1))$ for $n >= 2$. Then $(B_n)$ is a disjoint collection in $cal(F)$ with $union.big_n B_n = union.big_n A_n$, and $B_n subset.eq A_n$ for every $n$. Countable additivity therefore gives
$
  PP(union.big A_n) = PP(union.big B_n) = sum_n PP(B_n) <= sum_n PP(A_n).
$
